            <ArticleTitle>Copper-Catalyzed Carbenoid Insertion Reactions of α-Diazoesters and α-Diazoketones into Si-H and S-H Bonds.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3000-3010</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.6b02998</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient copper-catalyzed carbenoid insertion reaction of α-diazo carbonyl compounds into Si-H and S-H bonds was developed. A wide range of α-silylesters and α-thioesters was obtained in high yields (up to 98%) from α-diazoesters using 5 mol% of a simple copper(I) salt as catalyst. Using 0.05 mol% of the same catalyst, α-diazoketones led to α-silylketones in low to good yields (up to 70%).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
